# {{SLUG}} below = this agent's folder name - `make schedule ARGS="--all"` prints
# ready-made lines with everything already substituted; prefer that.
# Scheduling {{SLUG}} with cron (Linux, and macOS if the machine stays awake).
#
# Install:  crontab -e     then paste the lines you want.
# Check:    crontab -l
# Logs:     tail -f {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log
#
# This file only ever shows the ONE main loop as an example. If
# config/agent.yaml has a `schedule:` block (most agents in this family do -
# check yours), it lists every recurring job this agent actually needs, each
# with its own real command and cadence - print all of them, already filled
# in with the right absolute paths for THIS machine, with:
#
#     make schedule ARGS="--all"
#
# Paste that output into crontab -e instead of hand-editing the line below.
# `make schedule` on its own (or with --command/--cadence) generates one
# snippet for any single command you name:
#
#     make schedule ARGS="--cadence every-15-min"
#     make schedule ARGS="--command 'tools/run.py --once' --cadence every-5-min"
#
# cron starts with almost no environment, so both paths below MUST be absolute.
# Replace {{REPO_PATH}} with the output of `pwd` in this folder.

# Main loop, every 15 minutes - change the cadence to match what README.md
# and config/agent.yaml actually document for this agent.
*/15 * * * * cd {{REPO_PATH}} && {{REPO_PATH}}/.venv/bin/python tools/run.py --once >> {{REPO_PATH}}/data/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Start in shadow mode. Only add a schedule after you have watched a few real
# passes by hand and worked the review queue.
